# Verify code updates with tests

When you create or modify application code in this repo:

1. Run tests before finishing: `python -m pytest tests/ -q --tb=short`.
2. If tests fail, tell the user clearly what failed and fix when possible.
3. Do not claim the change is done while tests are failing.
4. Skip full-suite runs only for docs-only / comment-only edits; say so briefly.
5. A `stop` hook may also re-run tests and inject failures automatically — treat that output as authoritative and fix it.
